/farmland-atlas/kansas/pratt-county"],["ARC or PLC in Pratt County","/arc-plc/kansas/pratt-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, Pratt County&rsquo;s record runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids November to December came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle saw February to March at 22% of normal and August to September at 157%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 26% of normal on the middle. Grid 20824 had its driest year in 1956 at 43%.</p>"}
